			"notes": "## 0.3.0-beta – First Fabric release (Minecraft 26.3)\n\n**New**\n- Ported to **Fabric 26.3** (requires Fabric API)\n- New categories: **Headgear** (e.g. Halo) and **Face**\n- Cosmetics are attached to head or body based on their catalog data\n- Adjustable **offset** (e.g. halo height) is now applied\n- Capes are now drawn by the vanilla cape renderer, including its movement\n\n**Fixed**\n- **Glow**: glowing parts now light up like in LabyMod (incl. Angel Wings, Halo)\n- Worn colors are read correctly: offset values were mistaken for colors on 113 cosmetics\n- Failed downloads are retried instead of staying broken until restart\n\n**Improved**\n- Much less work per frame when many players wear cosmetics\n- Test mode only works in the development environment\n\nThe NeoForge 1.21.1 version remains available separately.\n\n*Not affiliated with LabyMod / LabyMedia GmbH.*\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/zXobic/LabyCosBri/commits/v0.3.0-beta+26.3"
		},
